<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What the accessibility service is allowed to see, declared as narrowly as the job permits.

  This file is read by Play review as much as by the platform, so every widening here needs a
  reason that survives being asked about.

  `accessibilityEventTypes` is an explicit list rather than `typeAllMask`. The mask is the
  default people reach for and it subscribes to view clicks, scrolls, selections, hover, window
  content changes and notifications - a vastly larger surveillance surface than this needs. The
  three types below are the minimum: text changing is the signal, focus tells us which field
  owns it, and window state tells us the conversation ended.

  `canRetrieveWindowContent` is the genuinely powerful flag and there is no way to avoid it: the
  text of a field is window content. It is what MonitoredField's password checks exist to
  constrain, since the flag itself cannot be scoped to "only fields that are not passwords".

  `flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows` is what lets the service find the keyboard's own window and
  place the warning exactly on top of it - the whole "overlay on the existing keyboard" design
  rests on this one flag. Without it the overlay falls back to a fixed offset and the shade
  cannot be positioned at all.

  `packageNames` is deliberately absent, which means every app. An allow-list of messaging apps
  would be the obvious narrowing and it fails in both directions: it misses whichever app a
  teenager moved to last month - precisely the one a grooming conversation migrates to - and it
  breaks silently when an app changes its package name. The narrowing that actually works is by
  kind of field, and that is done in code, in MonitoredField.

  `notificationTimeout` is 50ms rather than 0. Text-changed events arrive per keystroke and a
  zero timeout delivers every single one; 50ms coalesces a fast typist's burst into one scan
  without ever being slow enough to notice. The local scan is ~130us, so this is about event
  volume rather than scan cost.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeViewTextChanged|typeViewFocused|typeWindowStateChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows|flagIncludeNotImportantViews"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_service_description"
    android:notificationTimeout="50"
    android:summary="@string/accessibility_service_summary" />
